# The image is packaging only — the Dockerfile compiles nothing, it copies an already-built
# linux binary (see Dockerfile and the `krypton` / `docker` targets in the Makefile).
#
# So the build context is exactly one directory. Excluding everything and re-including dist/
# is deliberate rather than an enumeration of unwanted paths: it means adding a large directory
# to the repository later cannot silently start shipping it to the daemon, and the context
# stays a few tens of megabytes instead of the whole tree plus vendor/ and web/ui/node_modules.
*
!dist/
